| --- |

| **Q-17** Motion sensors should be placed in areas where traffic is unexpected, like server rooms, rather than high-traffic hallways — explain why placing motion sensors in high-traffic areas undermines their effectiveness, and connect this to the concept of alert fatigue that appears in Topic 1.5 when discussing AI-powered security systems. |
| --- |

| **Q-18** The framework notes that stationary guards protect specific areas while patrolling guards are more difficult for adversaries to plan around — analyze the trade-offs between these two deployment strategies, and describe a scenario where a combination of both would be more effective than either approach alone. *💬  Ask your AI: **"**What is security theater, and how can an organization accidentally implement it through poor placement of physical security controls?**"* |
| --- |

